    "text": "For H<sub>2</sub>S ; <math> <mrow> <msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></math> , <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>K</mtext> <msub> <mtext>a</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </msub> <mo>=</mo> <mn>1</mn> <msup> <mn>0</mn> <mrow> <mo>-</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math> . A Saturated solution of H<sub>2</sub> S in 0.1 M H<sub>2</sub>S contains Mn<sup>2</sup><sup> +</sup> , Co<sup>2</sup><sup> +</sup> and Ag<sup>+</sup> at an original concentration of 0.01 M each. Determine the pH range for selective precipitation of these metal ions<br />\r<br />\r<math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2.5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>21</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6.3</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mrow><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>50</mn></mrow></msup></math><br />\r<br />\rCalculate difference in pH for precipitation of Mns and CoS.",
